  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 60af0432a3c869e48a591344a8dafd71, type: 3}
  m_Name: CareDisc 1
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  question: "At a caregiver support group, you open up to a fellow caregiver and
    friend about your husband\u2019s side effects from the current treatment, which
    have made it hard for him to keep up with work and family life.  Your friend
    suggests you attend an upcoming discussion hosted by a cancer research center,
    explaining, \u201CIn early research, caregivers can help research teams understand
    how cancer and current treatments affect everyday life, even before a new treatment
    is tested in people.\u201D\n\nIs this true or false?"
  explanation: "Caregivers can share personal experiences that highlight real-world
    challenges. These insights help scientists design research that focuses on treatments
    that fit more smoothly into patients\u2019 lives. By learning about the daily
    struggles and successes families face, researchers can better understand what
    makes treatments hard \u2014 or helpful \u2014 in everyday life. This kind of
    input ensures early research keeps real people, not just lab results, at the
    center of discovery."
  correctAnswer: True
  incorrectAnswer1: False
  incorrectAnswer2: 
  incorrectAnswer3: 
  questionRole: Caregiver
  questionType: TrueFalse
  questionStage: Discovery
